        "abstract": "Advances in understanding the dielectric properties of biological substances continue to suffer from sporadic flurries of activity in specific areas that change with temporary fashion. In 1970 there was a relative preponderance of effort on thin lipid layers constructed as analogues to cellular membranes. Some work on proteins, polypeptides and whole cells was also reported. Most of these studies attempt to use dielectric data for structure analysis, a most difficult and often inconclusive procedure.",
