        "abstract": "The chapter is arranged in six sections. The first section entitled Primary Properties includes conventional investigations of intrinsic electric strength, thermal breakdown, breakdown of thin films and breakdown in situations which do not involve interaction with ambient media, e. g., laser-induced breakdown. The content of the other sections is evident from their titles. Considerable effort, as in previous years, has been concentrated upon the study of tracking and flashover of polluted insulation but a solution to this problem remains elusive. Interesting developments appear to be the impregnation of polythene by electro-negative gases in order to improve its electric properties. There is also the use of impregnated polymer film and paper-polymer composites in capacitor insulation which permit very appreciable increases in working stress.",
